<resources>
    <!--
      Hebrew.

      The folder is values-iw, NOT values-he. Hebrew's ISO code changed from
      "iw" to "he" in 1989 but Android still resolves the legacy code, and a
      values-he folder is silently ignored on older devices — the app simply
      falls back to English with no error anywhere. This is the single most
      common way an Android Hebrew translation ships and does nothing.

      Dashboard names, slugs and probe values stay English on purpose: they are
      identifiers, and translating them would make the app and the web console
      disagree about what a thing is called.
    -->
